rtz seeks another term in Indiana's 5th District, a seat with an R+8 partisan lean, against Democratic state senator J.D. Ford. Spartz has out-raised Ford overall, though Ford holds a cash-on-hand advantage after her heavy primary spending. Expert ratings lean Republican, with several outlets calling the race Safe R and others Likely R, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a 15% chance.\n\nDemocrats have targeted the district, and a July poll from a Democratic-sponsored firm showed a narrow two-point race, but that survey is dated and carries limited weight. Local coverage has focused on data centers, healthcare, and Spartz's calls for federal review of Indiana projects. The race remains Likely Republican, with Ford needing a strong national environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1386, "margin": -8.0}]}